But they also have erred through wine, and through strong drink are out of the way; the priest and the prophet have erred through strong drink, they are swallowed up of wine, they are out of the way through strong drink; they err in vision, they stumble in judgment.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQFor all tables are full of vomit and filthiness, so that there is no place clean.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verse	ªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWhom shall he teach knowledge? and whom shall he make to understand doctrine? them that are weaned from the milk, and drawn from the breasts.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzFor precept must be upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, and there a little:¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIfor with stammering lips and another tongue will he speak to this people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€To whom he said, This is the rest wherewith ye may cause the weary to rest; and this is the refreshing: yet they would not hear.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙâBut the word of the LORD was unto them precept upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, and there a little; that they might go, and fall backward, and be broken, and snared, and taken.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbWherefore hear the word of the LORD, ye scornful men, that rule this people which is in Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙõBecause ye have said, We have made a covenant with death, and with hell are we at agreement; when the overflowing scourge shall pass through, it shall not come unto us: for we have made lies our refuge, and under falsehood have we hid ourselves:¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµtherefore thus saith the Lord GOD, Behold, I lay in Zion for a foundation a stone, a tried stone, a precious corner stone, a sure foundation: he that believeth shall not make haste.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©Judgment also will I lay to the line, and righteousness to the plummet: and the hail shall sweep away the refuge of lies, and the waters shall overflow the hiding place.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶And your covenant with death shall be disannulled, and your agreement with hell shall not stand; when the overflowing scourge shall pass through, then ye shall be trodden down by it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®From the time that it goeth forth it shall take you: for morning by morning shall it pass over, by day and by night: and it shall be a vexation only to understand the report.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€For the bed is shorter than that a man can stretch himself on it: and the covering narrower than that he can wrap himself in it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´For the LORD shall rise up as in mount Perazim, he shall be wroth as in the valley of Gibeon, that he may do his work, his strange work; and bring to pass his act, his strange act.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡Now therefore be ye not mockers, lest your bands be made strong: for I have heard from the Lord GOD of hosts a consumption, even determined upon the whole earth.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<Give ye ear, and hear my voice; hearken, and hear my speech.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUDoth the plowman plow all day to sow? doth he open and break the clods of his ground?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»When he hath made plain the face thereof, doth he not cast abroad the fitches, and scatter the cummin, and cast in the principal wheat and the appointed barley and the rie in their place?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@For his God doth instruct him to discretion, and doth teach him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»For the fitches are not threshed with a threshing instrument, neither is a cart wheel turned about upon the cummin; but the fitches are beaten out with a staff, and the cummin with a rod.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠBread corn is bruised; because he will not ever be threshing it, nor break it with the wheel of his cart, nor bruise it with his horsemen.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgThis also cometh forth from the LORD of hosts, which is wonderful in counsel, and excellent in working.¦layout ªlast_verse